<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="196" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Gate Decision Record job: a refused processing lock is a Failure (redelivered, then dead-lettered), never a silent Success</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (185 dev check fixes)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies .cs code and tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>One located defect in one handler with a clear contract and an existing test rig.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>185-fixes</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches only GateDecisionRecordJob.cs and its test file; no other open task touches them.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, job, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Defect in our own task 149 code on master, found by ebilling-r1 during their 084h-3 review (2026-11-17); owner chose "Fix it now" (2026-11-17). `GateDecisionRecordJobHandler.ProcessAsync` returns `JobOutcome.Success` when `TryAcquireProcessingLockAsync` refuses the decision's lock. A refused lock is not proof that a record exists or will exist. Concrete loss path: attempt 1 fails (a Dataverse fault returns Failure and the message is abandoned), its lock release in the finally block hits a cache fault (IdempotencyService swallows it), and the broker redelivers the SAME message (same JobId = same lock owner) within `IdempotencyService.OwnerTakeoverAge` (1 minute). The redelivery is refused, completes as Success, and the gate decision never gets its Decision Record. Nothing is logged above Information and nothing is dead-lettered.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core, ADR-004 Service Bus job handlers and the BFF idempotency service.</role>
  <goal>A refused processing lock makes the job return `JobOutcome.Failure`: the processor abandons it for redelivery and, on the final delivery, dead-letters it (visible, replayable). A concurrent duplicate whose sibling wrote the record finds it on redelivery and completes as "already recorded". No path completes a gate job without a record except the D-144 by-design skips that exist today.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>
- Handler: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/GateDecisionRecordJob.cs`, `ProcessAsync` ~200-280 at origin/master `3c9a2ff4e1`. The refused branch is ~215-222. The class remarks (~148-160) say "a duplicate in flight [is] Success": update that sentence to the new rule.
- Lock semantics: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs` ~90-135 (acquire fails OPEN on a cache fault; same owner takes over only at least 1 minute later) and ~201-225 (owner release swallows faults). Do NOT change IdempotencyService (shared by many handlers).
- Processor: `Services/Jobs/ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs` ~210-240: Completed completes; Poisoned or `job.IsFinalDelivery` dead-letters; otherwise abandon (immediate redelivery). `JobContract.MaxDeliveryCount` = 5, `IsFinalDelivery` (JobContract.cs ~82).
- Reference: ebilling-r1's 084h-3 repair job (reviewed by us 2026-11-17 at `36b3f9004f`) returns Failure on a refused lock; same rule here.
- Tests: `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Signals/GateDecisionRecordJobTests.cs`. `AJobWhileAnotherJobHoldsTheSameDecision_WritesNothing_AndCompletes_TheLockNarrowsTheRace` (~177) asserts the old Success and must change; extend the existing Rig, do not build a new one.
- Line numbers are at origin/master `3c9a2ff4e1`; re-grep before editing.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/GateDecisionRecordJob.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Signals/GateDecisionRecordJobTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change this task makes to Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md. No new endpoint, DI registration, package, refusal reason or telemetry instrument. Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build and record it in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Change only the refused-lock branch and the remarks that describe it. Every other outcome of the handler (Poisoned paths, D-144 skips, Failure paths, the finally release) is unchanged; their existing tests pass unmodified.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The refused branch never releases the lock (it does not hold it) and never calls the writer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Logging on the refused branch: Warning with the job id, communication id, authorize flag, attempt and delivery count; on the final delivery (`job.IsFinalDelivery`) log Error saying the job will be dead-lettered and count it once with the existing `OntologyWriterTelemetry.RecordFailure(DecisionRecordRefusalReason.GateRecordFailed)`. Ids and gate values only (D-123).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">The fix stays inside the handler's outcome contract (Success / Failure / Poisoned); no change to ServiceBusJobProcessor, JobContract or IdempotencyService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target. Never run the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests; filter on GateDecisionRecordJobTests (and IdempotencyService tests if touched, which they must not be).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No deploy in this task. The fix reaches dev only through uac-r2's next dev BFF build.</constraint>
  </constraints>
