  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read ProcessAsync, the class remarks, IdempotencyService's acquire/release and the processor's outcome handling.</step>
    <step order="2">Change the refused-lock branch to return Failure with the logging and final-delivery metering in the constraints; update the remarks.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the tests in the acceptance criteria; prove the own-leftover-lock test fails on the old code (seeding proof: this guard prevents silent data loss).</step>
    <step order="4">Run the filtered tests, `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests` and `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` on the changed files. Record the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md status to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`. Record deviations and known limits in notes/task-196-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Test (seeding proof): a redelivery of the same job (same JobId) that finds its own earlier attempt's lock younger than OwnerTakeoverAge (the earlier release failed) returns Failed, writes nothing, logs at Warning, and leaves the lock in place. Against the old code it returns Completed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test: the same redelivery once the lock is at least OwnerTakeoverAge old takes the lock over and writes exactly one record (Completed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test: a second job (different JobId) for the same decision while the first holds the lock returns Failed and writes nothing; the first completes and writes exactly one record; a redelivery of the second after that completes as "already recorded" with no second record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test: a refused lock on the final delivery (`IsFinalDelivery` true) returns Failed, logs at Error and counts GateRecordFailed exactly once; on a non-final delivery it counts nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every other existing GateDecisionRecordJobTests test passes unmodified (only the old refused-lock test changes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build clean; ArchTests pass; dotnet format clean on changed files; publish-size delta recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a correct fix needs a change to IdempotencyService, JobContract or ServiceBusJobProcessor, STOP and report the options.</trigger>
    <trigger>If another job handler relies on the gate job completing on a refused lock, STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
